Qt / PySide6 (LGPL-3.0)
-----------------------
The bundled GUI toolkit (Qt, via PySide6) is used under the terms of the
GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 (LGPL-3.0); the license texts are in
the "Third-Party Licenses" tab of Help > Licenses and in third_party_license.txt. The Qt libraries
are separate files in the application folder (the PySide6 folder inside _internal,
or inside the macOS app bundle), not compiled into the program, and the
application loads them at runtime, so they can be replaced with a compatible build
of the same Qt version. The complete source code of Teacher's Teammate is publicly
available at https://github.com/JoHoenk/teachers-teammate.

The build carries only the Qt modules the app uses. The others (Qt Charts, Qt Quick 3D, ...) stay
out to keep the download small, and the smoke test fails if one is in the finished bundle.

FFmpeg inside OpenCV (LGPL-2.1)
-------------------------------
The OpenCV package (opencv-python-headless) carries FFmpeg. It is used under the GNU Lesser
General Public License, version 2.1, whose text is in the OpenCV entry of the third-party
license list. FFmpeg ships in the Linux and macOS bundles
only: the Windows bundle leaves out the separate DLL that OpenCV's Windows build carries.

libiconv inside lxml (LGPL-2.1)
-------------------------------
The lxml package links libiconv statically, for character-set conversion, under the GNU Lesser
General Public License, version 2.1; its text is in the lxml entry of the third-party license list
(the LICENSES.txt of the wheel). A statically linked library cannot be replaced with a compatible
build of its own, so section 6(a) of that license asks for the source of libiconv and for the
source of lxml, the work that links it in; both are named below.

Source code
-----------
The source of Teacher's Teammate itself is the "Source code" archive on the page of each release
(https://github.com/JoHoenk/teachers-teammate/releases).

The LGPL and MPL components above are open source, and this section says where their source
is. The Qt, PySide6, FFmpeg, libiconv, lxml and OpenCV entries name the version they were written
for; a bump turns the license test red until the entry and the sources release below name the new
one. certifi's entry names no version of its own: MPL-2.0 asks for the source of the version in
use, and its PyPI release is that source. The source of every other bundled package is its PyPI
release at the version in third_party_licenses/inventory.csv.

Qt 6.12.0 and PySide6 6.12.0, the versions the bundle carries:
  https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/6.12/6.12.0/submodules/
      (qtbase, qtsvg, qtimageformats, qtwayland)
  https://download.qt.io/official_releases/QtForPython/pyside6/PySide6-6.12.0-src/

FFmpeg 9.0.2, inside opencv-python-headless 5.1.0.95 (Linux and macOS):
  https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.gz
  The wheel's build recipe: https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python (tag 95)

libiconv 1.18, inside lxml 6.1.3 (Linux, Windows and macOS):
  https://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/libiconv/libiconv-1.18.tar.gz
  Its signature: https://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/libiconv/libiconv-1.18.tar.gz.sig
  lxml's own source, the work that links libiconv in: https://pypi.org/project/lxml/6.1.3/

certifi (MPL-2.0), the version Help > Licenses lists:
  https://pypi.org/project/certifi/

The same sources, as one download, are published with this release:
  https://github.com/JoHoenk/teachers-teammate/releases/tag/third-party-sources-qt6.12.0
It holds the four Qt modules above, pyside-setup at the matching tag, the FFmpeg and libiconv
tarballs with their signatures, and the opencv-python-headless and lxml sources. It is never the
"latest" release, so the app's update check does not see it.

Written offer
-------------
The sources release named above is the offer of corresponding source from the same place as the
download (GPL-3.0 section 6(d), as used through LGPL-3.0; LGPL-2.1 section 6(d) for FFmpeg and
libiconv). Teacher's Teammate itself is offered the same way: the "Source code" archive on the page
of each release is its Corresponding Source (GPL-3.0 section 6(d)).

The macOS OpenCV libraries and the Linux host libraries are covered by this offer. The Linux
download's third_party_host_libraries.txt names the Ubuntu source package and version of every
library the bundle took from the build machine.

Optional components
-------------------
Optional OCR, LLM, and privacy features (LangChain, spaCy, ...) are
not bundled. They are installed on demand and are governed by their own
licenses.

PaddleOCR algorithms
--------------------
The built-in reader's text-box post-processing and line cropping re-implement the published
algorithms of PaddleOCR (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR). No PaddleOCR
source code is included in this product. The model files the reader runs are third-party
components; their attribution and license text are in the third-party license report.

Installer artifacts
-------------------
Third-party code embedded in the platform installers (e.g. the NSIS stub in the
Windows setup.exe) is covered in tools/packaging/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
